  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the contrasting scenes of the meme",
  "description": "The user is not explicitly projected onto any single element via deictic pronouns like 'me' or 'you'. However, the meme's structure and intent create an implicit projection where the user is positioned as a viewer who is expected to interpret and align with the binary narrative presented — viewing the top scene as 'immigrants' (positive, integrated) and the bottom scene as 'illegal aliens' (negative, undesirable). This projection is onto the overall juxtaposition of scenes, which frames the user as someone who must make a judgment or take a side within the false dichotomy presented. The user is thus projected onto the 'meme_juxtaposition' scene, which is the central visual and conceptual unit of the meme.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
